  "tags": [
   "music"
  ],
  "html": "<p>Today, for the first time in my life, I heard a sound that Lana Del Rey once described as &rsquo;telephone wires above are sizzling like a snare&rsquo; in her Summertime Sadness. Though in my case, it wasn’t telephone wires but a power transmission line. Having been born and raised in a city, I’d never been close enough to power lines to hear them humming before. This experience boosted my mood, even if only for a little while.</p>\n<p><em>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@frimlat/114376841045321303\">Mastodon</a>.</em></p>",
